      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Successful recanalisation of a chronic coronary occlusion may result in survival advantage. This report describes a 61-year-old man with an initially chronic occluded right coronary artery. A follow-up angiography 2 years later revealed a spontaneous recanalisation."},
